    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "030a1ea6_8c97051f",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/vc/VolumeControlService.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 571,
      "author": {
        "id": 3256421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T10:36:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought that not, as it was used in setGroupVolume too. adjustDeviceMute is similar logic as in group but adopted to use with one device only.\n\nBut I checked it right now and notice that this warning from setGroupVolume is always logged when you go down volume to 0 using phone volume contrl button and again when goin up. So maybe we should change it in both places.\n\nAnother thing which I found in this test is that on Samsung Galaxy 2/3 Pro (on Sony XM5 did not shows) when you go with volume down or up you always get error log:\n```\nsystem/bta/vc/vc.cc:425 HandleAutonomusVolumeChange: Autonomous change but volume and mute did not changed.\n```\nor\n```\nsystem/bta/vc/vc.cc:923 RemoveDeviceFromOperationList: Could not find operation id: 288\n```\n\nAnd one more that Samsung Samsung Galaxy 2/3 Pro does not unmute so if go with volume to 0 using phone buttons and volume up by HS then it is still muted.\nHS issue which was very common on march UPF.\n\n@rlukasz@google.com Do you remember if this was reported to the Samsung? Should we fix smth on our side with logs severity?",
      "parentUuid": "d547b826_02ab7349",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 571,
        "startChar": 16,
        "endLine": 571,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "82b01636d0bd5154613d72f56ae2b93a3262f430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff545131_7fa4e336",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/vc/VolumeControlService.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-10T22:26:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You created this map as a concurrentHashMap but you are taking a lock anyway. What is the threading model here ? Why locking here but not locking line 556 ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "82b01636d0bd5154613d72f56ae2b93a3262f430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fa72bc89_34ce22dd",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/vc/VolumeControlService.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 3256421
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T10:36:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "synchronize is needed as when mGroupVolumeCache is changed we need to update mDeviceVolumeCache too so I want to be sure that it is done atomically.\n\nNevertheless in next CL I synchronized whole method because there was reces between AF/VCS/BothRemotes",
      "parentUuid": "ff545131_7fa4e336",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "82b01636d0bd5154613d72f56ae2b93a3262f430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b095e69_f36cc63f",
        "filename": "android/app/src/com/android/bluetooth/vc/VolumeControlService.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 598,
      "author": {
        "id": 1881060
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T20:21:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e  I want to be sure that it is done atomically.\n\nMake sens, but in that case you want to annotate your variable with `@GuardedBy`, that way you will have report at compile time of the variable being accessed outside of the lock\n\n\n\n---\n\n---\n\n\n\nSomehow related but not 100% related:\n\nI had a change to fix all possible race in vcp with aosp/3379907, the change consist in making run everything on one thread.\n\nBut it need to be re-done due to the huge amount of merge conflicts",
      "parentUuid": "fa72bc89_34ce22dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 598,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 598,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "82b01636d0bd5154613d72f56ae2b93a3262f430",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
